WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.179 --> 00:00:04.606
Let's talk about the demi-gods, who are each
and all the direct offspring of Queen Marika.

00:00:04.606 --> 00:00:06.067
There was Godwyn

00:00:06.067 --> 00:00:06.997
Morgott

00:00:06.997 --> 00:00:08.000
Mohg

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:09.000
Radahn

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:10.000
Rykard.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:11.000
Ranni.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:13.189
Miquella, and Malenia, Blade
of Miquella.

00:00:13.189 --> 00:00:20.150
Malenia, Blade of Miquella

00:00:20.150 --> 00:00:24.780
all of these demi-gods had fallen from grace
by the time the shattering occurred, but in

00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:29.000
this video I want to mostly talk about the
origins of these characters.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:31.910
Who these demi-gods were, before the fall.

00:00:31.910 --> 00:00:37.470
...and some of these demi-gods fell a long
way, indeed.

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:42.300
Before he became this unsightly mess Godwyn
the Golden was quite the heroic figure.

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:47.840
He was born of the promising union between
Lord Godfrey and Queen Marika, and achieved

00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:53.840
great renown for his bravery in one of their
wars: The War of the Ancient Dragons.

00:00:53.840 --> 00:01:00.390
This war began when Gransax, a great ancient
dragon, rained calamity down upon Leyndell,

00:01:00.390 --> 00:01:05.740
marking the only time in historical record
that the Royal Capital's walls had fallen

00:01:05.740 --> 00:01:11.360
It's not clear why Gransax first attacked
- but, fortifying themselves against lightning,

00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:16.450
the knights of the Erdtree weathered his assault,
and Gransax was defeated However, this was

00:01:16.450 --> 00:01:21.939
only the beginning - and a bitter war against
the Ancient Dragons was to follow.

00:01:21.939 --> 00:01:28.140
During this war, the Erdtree Sentinels had
an epiphany: that "The only way to truly protect

00:01:28.140 --> 00:01:31.630
the Erdtree, was to become dragons themselves".

00:01:31.630 --> 00:01:37.630
And so, despoiling the corpses of their foes,
the grotesque sentinels served the Erdtree,,

00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:40.970
- but fought with the claws of the enemy instead

00:01:40.970 --> 00:01:44.310
In the end, the Ancient Dragons were routed
once again.

00:01:44.310 --> 00:01:49.520
In a graveyard of swords by the Stormcaller
Church, the end of the war is commemorated.

00:01:49.520 --> 00:01:55.970
Here, we learn that, during battle, Godwyn
the Golden defeated Fortissax, the mightiest

00:01:55.970 --> 00:01:57.410
dragon of them all.

00:01:57.410 --> 00:02:00.460
However, he did not kill Fortissax.

00:02:00.460 --> 00:02:03.110
Instead, he befriended him.

00:02:03.110 --> 00:02:08.039
And it was in this act, that the powers of
the ancient dragons truly became a part of

00:02:08.039 --> 00:02:14.060
Leyndell - after all, "only those loved by
dragons can survive the ordeal of cladding

00:02:14.060 --> 00:02:16.099
their bodies in lightning".

00:02:16.099 --> 00:02:21.769
So from an unlikely friendship, an ancient
dragon cult was born in the capital city,

00:02:21.769 --> 00:02:26.459
and the knights of Leyndell learned to worship
the dragons, and wield their lightning.

00:02:26.459 --> 00:02:32.370
Lansseax, sister of Fortissax, even took human
form to better commune with the knights . it

00:02:32.370 --> 00:02:37.559
was officially decided that worship of the
ancient dragons did not conflict with belief

00:02:37.559 --> 00:02:38.659
in the Erdtree... -

00:02:38.659 --> 00:02:44.440
and it was all thanks to Godwyn - commander
of the dragon's "Golden" lightning, and a

00:02:44.440 --> 00:02:48.189
true child of the Golden Lineage.

00:02:48.189 --> 00:02:54.519
But now...let's talk about Morgott, and Mohg,
the Omen twins who were also born of Godfrey

00:02:54.519 --> 00:02:56.930
and Marika's Golden Lineage.

00:02:56.930 --> 00:02:58.809
First, what is an Omen?

00:02:58.809 --> 00:03:05.790
Well, to put it simply, an Omen is an "accursed"
child, seen as "impure", as they are born

00:03:05.790 --> 00:03:08.389
with horns on the body and face.

00:03:08.389 --> 00:03:13.870
When this happens, the correct thing to do,
culturally, is to cut off the horns of the

00:03:13.870 --> 00:03:18.839
Omen, an act which usually causes them to
perish It's pretty messed up.

00:03:18.839 --> 00:03:27.359
Now some Omen do survive this process - and
some are even given the Omen Cleaver, a weapon

00:03:27.359 --> 00:03:33.909
awarded as a tool of war, though these weapons
are bestowed with a readiness to take them

00:03:33.909 --> 00:03:34.909
away

00:03:34.909 --> 00:03:40.150
We find one such Omen in an Erdtree camp upon
the Altus Plateau.

00:03:40.150 --> 00:03:45.359
Before you fight it, you might have noticed
another Omen writhing in its sleep.

00:03:45.359 --> 00:03:50.309
It's said that Omen see evil spirits in their
nightmares, and I think this Omen is dreaming

00:03:50.309 --> 00:03:55.010
- haunted, by the vengeful spirits of its
accursed kin.

00:03:55.010 --> 00:04:01.400
This brings us to the Omenkillers, horrifying
butchers of twisted conscience, who wear horned

00:04:01.400 --> 00:04:08.019
masks that make a mockery of the Omens' nightmares'
. These butchers hunt Omen, and amputate their

00:04:08.019 --> 00:04:09.180
horns.

00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:16.669
The first Omenkiller was named Rollo - a famous
perfumer who imbibed a physick that rid himself

00:04:16.669 --> 00:04:23.129
of emotion, so that he could better perform
his tasks . Remember, many Omen have their

00:04:23.129 --> 00:04:26.629
horns excised when they're only babies.

00:04:26.629 --> 00:04:32.050
That's..definitely disturbing enough to warrant
a emotion-killing physick, in my book.

00:04:32.050 --> 00:04:38.870
However, if the Omen is born of royalty, then
their horns are not cut off, but they are

00:04:38.870 --> 00:04:43.699
"kept underground, unbeknownst to anyone,
and imprisoned for eternity".

00:04:43.699 --> 00:04:48.349
By way of example, you would have seen all
kinds of horned Omen confined to the sewers

00:04:48.349 --> 00:04:49.810
beneath Leyndell.

00:04:49.810 --> 00:04:56.520
But why are the Omen considered to be accursed
in the first place?

00:04:56.520 --> 00:05:01.360
What's inherently wrong with being born with
horns and great strength?

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:07.240
Well..it's important to remember that this
curse might only really exist in the context

00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:12.680
of the Golden Order - after all, those afflicted
with omen horns are not able to return to

00:05:12.680 --> 00:05:17.880
the Erdtree for rebirth, and are born outside
of its grace.

00:05:17.880 --> 00:05:22.210
And why does the Golden Order disavow the
Omen?

00:05:22.210 --> 00:05:27.919
Well it's hard to say for sure, but it's my
working theory that it's to do with the crucible.

00:05:27.919 --> 00:05:33.370
According to this ancient incantation, "horns"
were once an aspect of the Erdtree's primordial

00:05:33.370 --> 00:05:36.759
crucible, where all life was once blended
together.

00:05:36.759 --> 00:05:41.889
. And with the exception of a couple of crucible
knights in and around Leyndell, we know the

00:05:41.889 --> 00:05:47.090
Golden Order has started to distance itself
from anything that touches upon the crucible.

00:05:47.090 --> 00:05:53.220
While things like horns, knots, feathers and
scales once grew on the human body and were

00:05:53.220 --> 00:05:59.469
considered signifiers of the divine , now
they are disdained as impurities, as civilization

00:05:59.469 --> 00:06:01.130
has "advanced".

00:06:01.130 --> 00:06:06.669
We learn this from the knot, scale and feather
talismans - all of which are guarded by Omen,

00:06:06.669 --> 00:06:09.110
or dropped by Omenkillers, no less.

00:06:09.110 --> 00:06:14.330
Unfortunately for the Order of the Erdtree,
these once-divine "impurities" seem to crop

00:06:14.330 --> 00:06:17.919
up in some births, whether they like it or
not.

00:06:17.919 --> 00:06:23.040
Almost like it's a genetic trait..as if it
touches on the crucible at the root of the

00:06:23.040 --> 00:06:24.040
Erdtree.

00:06:24.040 --> 00:06:28.620
And so...you have to ask - is it really a
curse to be born as a graceless Omen?

00:06:28.620 --> 00:06:34.500
Well, as with most curses in these games,
I think that depends on your perspective.

00:06:34.500 --> 00:06:40.960
In any case, Mohg and Morgott were Omen royalty,
and thus, were born into a wretched mire far

00:06:40.960 --> 00:06:43.240
below the earth, horns and all.

00:06:43.240 --> 00:06:48.569
Here, they were kept under the strictest confinement
- each of them with charmed shackles that

00:06:48.569 --> 00:06:53.879
were covered in roots , and bathed in golden
magic.

00:06:53.879 --> 00:06:57.060
It seems very few people were supposed to
know that they even existed .

00:06:57.060 --> 00:07:03.499
Morgott, for his part, renounced and despised
his accursed Omen blood - but his brother

00:07:03.499 --> 00:07:05.560
Mohg embraced it.

00:07:05.560 --> 00:07:10.669
Deep underground, Mohg stood before an outer
god - a being called the Formless Mother,

00:07:10.669 --> 00:07:15.620
who craves wounds, and was capable of bestowing
power upon accursed blood.

00:07:15.620 --> 00:07:20.120
In this moment, Mohg's accursed blood erupted
with fire, and he became besotted with the

00:07:20.120 --> 00:07:22.330
defilement that he was born into.

00:07:22.330 --> 00:07:27.460
Here, deep below the earth, he would go on
to build a dynasty of blood, in reverence

00:07:27.460 --> 00:07:31.229
of a mother - something that it seems he never
truly had.

00:07:31.229 --> 00:07:35.879
As for Morgott, he was born into the same
accursed fate as his twin brother - but despite

00:07:35.879 --> 00:07:40.620
not being blessed with grace, he loved the
Erdtree all the same, and even took it upon

00:07:40.620 --> 00:07:45.120
himself to crawl out of the sewers and become
the Erdtree's protector , when the Erdtree

00:07:45.120 --> 00:07:46.740
needed him most.

00:07:46.740 --> 00:07:50.389
In the end, he rightfully became the Omen
King, and Lord of Leyndell.

00:07:50.389 --> 00:07:56.030
Omen or not, he was, after all, born of Godfrey
and Marika's Golden Lineage.

00:07:56.030 --> 00:08:02.450
Of course, the marriage between Godfrey and
Marika would be ended, and before long, Marika

00:08:02.450 --> 00:08:09.729
remarried with another man - a champion, named
Radagon, who Marika calls her "other half"

00:08:09.729 --> 00:08:15.059
. He became second Elden Lord, and the King
Consort, but he also brought with him three

00:08:15.059 --> 00:08:22.550
children from a previous marriage with a Carian
Queen named Rennala.These children were Ranni,

00:08:22.550 --> 00:08:30.289
Rykard, and Radahn, and they became demigod
stepchildren after Radagon's (re?)Union with

00:08:30.289 --> 00:08:31.689
Queen Marika.

00:08:31.689 --> 00:08:37.570
Possessed of his father's flaming red hair,
Radahn was fond of its heroic implications,

00:08:37.570 --> 00:08:40.120
and considered himself to be born of a great
champion.

00:08:40.120 --> 00:08:45.370
Yet, he had also long looked up to another
man - Godfrey, the First Elden Lord: Queen

00:08:45.370 --> 00:08:48.660
Marika's first husband, and the Lord of the
Battlefield.

00:08:48.660 --> 00:08:53.720
But Radahn wasn't just the son of Radagon
and an aspiring Lord of the Battlefield..he

00:08:53.720 --> 00:08:59.070
was also the son of Rennala, who was head
of the Academy of Raya Lucaria, and Queen

00:08:59.070 --> 00:09:00.070
of Caria.

00:09:00.070 --> 00:09:06.300
So, as a Carian royal inclined towards sorcery,
Radahn bent his will towards mastering gravitational

00:09:06.300 --> 00:09:07.459
magics.

00:09:07.459 --> 00:09:13.190
Rock Sling...Gravity Well..Collapsing Stars..these
techniques were taught to him in Sellia, the

00:09:13.190 --> 00:09:19.250
Town of Sorcery...all so he would never have
to abandon his beloved but scrawny steed.

00:09:19.250 --> 00:09:24.709
That said, before long, his powers would soon
be put towards a more...cosmic purpose than

00:09:24.709 --> 00:09:28.000
simply allowing him to ride his horse.

00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:33.079
Radahn was taught gravitational magic by an
Alabaster Lord - a member of "a race of ancients

00:09:33.079 --> 00:09:38.670
with skin of stone who were said to have risen
to life when a meteor struck long ago".

00:09:38.670 --> 00:09:42.889
And when his lessons were complete, Radahn
said these chilling words:

00:09:42.889 --> 00:09:47.180
"I thank you for your tutelage, for now I
can challenge the stars".

00:09:47.180 --> 00:09:52.390
And of course, he did conquer the stars - and
the very constellations would be halted by

00:09:52.390 --> 00:09:53.390
his strength.

00:09:53.390 --> 00:09:55.260
But of course..you have to ask..why?

00:09:55.260 --> 00:09:58.300
Why was it necessary to conquer the stars?

00:09:58.300 --> 00:10:01.540
Well I have a couple of theories.

00:10:01.540 --> 00:10:04.650
Theory 1 is that this was done in self defense.

00:10:04.650 --> 00:10:10.180
After all, according to the Sword Gravestone,
Radahn was "protecting Sellia".

00:10:10.180 --> 00:10:15.360
What's more, Gravitational magic has "destructive
power", AND many gravitational beasts are

00:10:15.360 --> 00:10:17.230
proof of that destructive power.

00:10:17.230 --> 00:10:22.380
A being named Astel had even come down to
the Lands Between in the past, and destroyed

00:10:22.380 --> 00:10:25.089
a place called the "Eternal City".

00:10:25.089 --> 00:10:30.160
What's more, Sellians are "descendants of
the Eternal", positioned right above the Eternal

00:10:30.160 --> 00:10:36.720
City underground - so there is an argument
to be made for Radahn purely defending Sellia,

00:10:36.720 --> 00:10:37.980
here.

00:10:37.980 --> 00:10:42.500
But it's possible for Radahn to have fought
in this conflict, AND to have made the first

00:10:42.500 --> 00:10:43.900
move as well.

00:10:43.900 --> 00:10:49.580
So this is theory 2 - that Radahn conquered
the stars as a preventative measure, in service

00:10:49.580 --> 00:10:51.509
to the Greater Will.

00:10:51.509 --> 00:10:55.930
According to a set of Astrologer items, the
night sky cradles fate.

00:10:55.930 --> 00:11:01.980
There's even a banished sect of people called
the "Nox", who live deep below the earth who

00:11:01.980 --> 00:11:07.660
live in eternal anticipation of the coming
age of the stars, and their Lord of Night.

00:11:07.660 --> 00:11:11.899
Long ago, these people invoked the ire of
the Greater Will.

00:11:11.899 --> 00:11:17.459
So it would make sense that those in service
to Greater Will might have sought to arrest

00:11:17.459 --> 00:11:20.270
the stars, and put an end to this fate.

00:11:20.270 --> 00:11:26.490
What's more, Radahn was a huge fanboy of Godfrey,
and seems to have more loyalty to the Erdtree,

00:11:26.490 --> 00:11:28.170
than to the moon.

00:11:28.170 --> 00:11:34.310
Most tellingly however, the Telescope says
that "the fate once writ in the night skies

00:11:34.310 --> 00:11:36.930
had been fettered by the Golden Order".

00:11:36.930 --> 00:11:41.470
Surely this is referring to Radahn's actions,
and it levels the blame blame at the Golden

00:11:41.470 --> 00:11:42.540
Order, rather than Radahn himself.

00:11:42.540 --> 00:11:47.870
But putting Radahn's motivations aside, it's
a fact that the stars were held back, and

00:11:47.870 --> 00:11:53.450
that this had great consequences for many..especially
for the rest of his Carian Royal family.

00:11:53.450 --> 00:11:55.400
Let me explain.

00:11:55.400 --> 00:12:00.019
The fate of the Carian royal family is guided
by the stars.

00:12:00.019 --> 00:12:06.529
As is the fate of Lady Ranni, first heir in
the Carian royal line.

00:12:06.529 --> 00:12:10.910
But General Radahn is the conqueror of the
stars.

00:12:10.910 --> 00:12:17.339
Who stood up to the swirling constellations,
halting their movement in a smashing victory.

00:12:17.339 --> 00:12:24.589
And so, if General Radahn were defeated, the
stars would once again resume their movement.

00:12:24.589 --> 00:12:29.089
As would Lady Ranni's destiny.

00:12:29.089 --> 00:12:35.000
Lunar Princess Ranni was the daughter of Radagon
and Rennala, and sister to Radahn.

00:12:35.000 --> 00:12:39.490
Interestingly, if you look at her true body
atop a divine tower - it looks like she might

00:12:39.490 --> 00:12:42.590
have also inherited the red hair of Radagon.

00:12:42.590 --> 00:12:44.029
Cool detail.

00:12:44.029 --> 00:12:50.570
But unlike Radahn, she quite clearly took
after her mother more, who was Rennala, head

00:12:50.570 --> 00:12:52.949
of the Carian Royal family.

00:12:52.949 --> 00:12:59.560
The house of Caria has a storied history - one
that seems to go way back to the astrologers.

00:12:59.560 --> 00:13:04.940
In the Carian Manor, we find one of their
treasures - the Sword of Night and Flame.

00:13:04.940 --> 00:13:10.430
It reads "Astrologers, who preceded the sorcerers,
established themselves in mountaintops that

00:13:10.430 --> 00:13:15.190
nearly touched the sky, and considered the
Fire Giants their neighbours".

00:13:15.190 --> 00:13:19.649
Rennala herself was an astrologer, always
chasing the stars, in her youth.

00:13:19.649 --> 00:13:26.310
Then, she met the full moon - and, in time,
the astrologer became a queen, establishing

00:13:26.310 --> 00:13:28.759
the House of Caria as royalty.

00:13:28.759 --> 00:13:35.139
Caria appears to have had a matriarchal heirarchy,
with multiple princesses, and Carian knights

00:13:35.139 --> 00:13:36.930
that served as their retainers.

00:13:36.930 --> 00:13:42.319
Now, however, there is only one princess:
Ranni, daughter of Rennala.

00:13:42.319 --> 00:13:47.170
And at the time of her birth, she would have
been set to inherit quite a lot of power indeed.

00:13:47.170 --> 00:13:52.610
For the Carian Royal Family was at its height,
and her mother was not only Queen - she was

00:13:52.610 --> 00:13:58.220
also head of the academy of Raya Lucaria,
having bewitched them with the enchanting

00:13:58.220 --> 00:14:00.860
power of the full moon.

00:14:00.860 --> 00:14:05.759
Leading the young Ranni by the hand, Rennala
guided her daughter to a meeting with a moon

00:14:05.759 --> 00:14:07.130
of her own.

00:14:07.130 --> 00:14:12.100
What Ranni beheld was cold, dark, and veiled
in occult mystery.

00:14:12.100 --> 00:14:16.410
A Dark Moon - a sort of twin to Rennala's
own full moon.

00:14:16.410 --> 00:14:21.190
You can even see both of these hanging in
the sky, if you stargaze from the heights

00:14:21.190 --> 00:14:23.420
of the Moonlight Plateau.

00:14:23.420 --> 00:14:29.040
Another who guided Ranni was a character called
the "snowy crone", who the young Ranni encountered

00:14:29.040 --> 00:14:30.430
deep in the woods.

00:14:30.430 --> 00:14:34.320
When you look at Ranni, it's actually the
likeness of this snow witch that you're seeing

00:14:34.320 --> 00:14:40.470
- as the doll that now houses Ranni's soul,
was modeled after her..probably as a sign

00:14:40.470 --> 00:14:41.610
of respect.

00:14:41.610 --> 00:14:44.890
Clearly, Ranni looked up to this mysterious
woman.

00:14:44.890 --> 00:14:50.241
She became the girl's secret mentor, and she
even knew about the dark moon - teaching the

00:14:50.241 --> 00:14:55.209
young Ranni to fear it as she imparted her
cold sorceries.

00:14:55.209 --> 00:14:57.450
So what do these moons represent?

00:14:57.450 --> 00:15:02.500
Now this is just a theory, but it seems that
moons act as guides.

00:15:02.500 --> 00:15:07.900
The lost black moon of Nokstella, for example,
"was the guide of countless stars".

00:15:07.900 --> 00:15:12.670
What's more, Ranni and Rennala were heavily
influenced by their moons: Rennala's moon

00:15:12.670 --> 00:15:17.890
bewitched the academy that she became the
head of, and Ranni's Dark Moon, for its part,

00:15:17.890 --> 00:15:22.759
also imparts "wisdom" and leads a "voyage",
in the Age of Stars ending.

00:15:22.759 --> 00:15:25.570
They could even be outer gods.

00:15:25.570 --> 00:15:31.459
And yet, for all this guidance, Caria - and
Liurnia as a whole, have experienced steep

00:15:31.459 --> 00:15:32.949
decline.

00:15:32.949 --> 00:15:35.459
Radagon betrayed the House of the Moon.

00:15:35.459 --> 00:15:37.740
Radahn locked the stars into motion.

00:15:37.740 --> 00:15:42.740
The Academy Town is flooded to the North,
Caria has been ruined in the west, and the

00:15:42.740 --> 00:15:45.459
stars and moon have gone their seperate ways.

00:15:45.459 --> 00:15:53.180
Nevertheless, Ranni, last princess of Caria
- remains - carefully setting new plans into

00:15:53.180 --> 00:15:54.950
motion.

00:15:54.950 --> 00:16:01.040
Sibling to Ranni and Radahn was a man named
Rykard, Lord of the Volcano manor.

00:16:01.040 --> 00:16:05.579
There is evidence that Rykard was friendly
with his siblings - he conspired with his

00:16:05.579 --> 00:16:12.009
sister Ranni, and there's even a portrait
of Radahn hung in the Volcano Manor..as well

00:16:12.009 --> 00:16:16.079
as a portrait of Rykard himself - before the
fall.

00:16:16.079 --> 00:16:21.430
Item descriptions mark Rykard as stern, heroic,
ambitious...and blasphemous.

00:16:21.430 --> 00:16:29.089
A part of this blasphemy was opposing the
Erdtree . which drew many knights to his banner.

00:16:29.089 --> 00:16:32.029
For Rykard believed in taking by force..

00:16:32.029 --> 00:16:37.839
just as the gods did..and clearly, many believed
he would usher in a new age.

00:16:37.839 --> 00:16:42.540
The armor set of the Gelmir Knights reveals
to us what were once very loyal soldiers.

00:16:42.540 --> 00:16:48.689
The crest of red feathers are there symbolize
Rykard's pedigree as Lord Radagon's son, and

00:16:48.689 --> 00:16:53.529
the emblem upon their chestpiece stands for
a lord with lofty ambitions.

00:16:53.529 --> 00:16:54.550
However...

00:16:54.550 --> 00:17:00.750
As Rykard delved into the ancient secrets
of Mount Gelmir, he came across the Immortal

00:17:00.750 --> 00:17:05.730
Great Serpent, an ancient deity that aligned
with Rykard's ambitions.

00:17:05.730 --> 00:17:13.490
And so, Rykard fed himself to the the Great
Serpent, so that he might devour, grow, and

00:17:13.490 --> 00:17:14.950
live eternally.

00:17:14.950 --> 00:17:21.000
Alas, this was too much for his knights, and
they believed that their masters heroic aspirations

00:17:21.000 --> 00:17:23.990
had degenerated into mere greed.

00:17:23.990 --> 00:17:29.060
So, they searched desperately for a weapon
with which they might halt their lord - and

00:17:29.060 --> 00:17:37.330
they found it too - a Serpent-Hunter spear
that had been used to hunt the immortal serpent

00:17:37.330 --> 00:17:39.370
in the distant past.

00:17:39.370 --> 00:17:41.060
But it was too late.

00:17:41.060 --> 00:17:46.530
As the lord lost his dignity, so too did these
knights, lose their master.

00:17:46.530 --> 00:17:54.060
Not that it bothered Rykard.

00:17:54.060 --> 00:17:58.460
Next, we need to discuss Malenia..and Miquella.

00:17:58.460 --> 00:18:00.950
These two were twins, as they were born TOGETHAA

00:18:00.950 --> 00:18:02.200
No..fuck off Rykard.

00:18:02.200 --> 00:18:03.440
Not your section.

00:18:03.440 --> 00:18:07.360
So - as you know Radagon's marriage with Rennala
did not last.

00:18:07.360 --> 00:18:11.770
Afterwards, he returned to the Golden Order,
and became Queen Marika's consort.

00:18:11.770 --> 00:18:16.900
But what I haven't yet mentioned is that together
(TOGETHAA), they were blessed with two demi-god

00:18:16.900 --> 00:18:17.900
children.

00:18:17.900 --> 00:18:20.250
Malenia, and Miquella, the so-called "twin
prodigies".

00:18:20.250 --> 00:18:26.430
Now, in the last lore video, I briefly proposed
that these two twins were born after the shattering,

00:18:26.430 --> 00:18:30.770
after Radagon and Marika had merged together
to become a single god.

00:18:30.770 --> 00:18:32.810
However, I've changed my mind.

00:18:32.810 --> 00:18:39.680
To put it simply, there's just too much proof
that Malenia and Miquella were a force influencing

00:18:39.680 --> 00:18:42.800
the world long before the shattering took
place .

00:18:42.800 --> 00:18:50.460
Anyway - both of the twins were born afflicted.

00:18:50.460 --> 00:18:56.320
Miquella was born "afflicted" with eternal
youth..and Malenia, for her part, was born

00:18:56.320 --> 00:18:58.120
"vulnerable" to Rot.

00:18:58.120 --> 00:19:01.550
Interestingly, Malenia's Scarlet Rot..is actually
an outer god, and old legends of the Scarlet

00:19:01.550 --> 00:19:02.550
Rot have persisted in the world for generations.

00:19:02.550 --> 00:19:06.860
This Outer God, like many others in the game,
seems to have an "order" that is able to be

00:19:06.860 --> 00:19:19.070
imposed upon the world via an empyrean vessel.

00:19:19.070 --> 00:19:25.920
According to Gowry, the "Order" of Rot is
resplendent - a cycle of death..and rebirth.

00:19:25.920 --> 00:19:31.030
Kind of like the lotus flower, that blooms
anew from the mud.

00:19:31.030 --> 00:19:34.320
I..actually have art of this, hanging in my
home.

00:19:34.320 --> 00:19:36.110
I always loved the symbol of it.

00:19:36.110 --> 00:19:42.270
I have lots of art hanging now actually, and
I'm going to talk about it at the end of the

00:19:42.270 --> 00:19:43.270
video.

00:19:43.270 --> 00:19:44.270
Anyway ~

00:19:44.270 --> 00:19:48.890
So Malenia the Empyrean was "vulnerable" to,
and "afflicted" by, the Scarlet Rot.

00:19:48.890 --> 00:19:55.380
There was said to be no cure, and while fire
and consecration seem to be somewhat effective

00:19:55.380 --> 00:20:01.290
at warding it off, Malenia would slowly lose
her physical self to the Rot.

00:20:01.290 --> 00:20:06.190
Interestingly, old legends of the Scarlet
Rot have persisted in the world for generations

00:20:06.190 --> 00:20:11.070
..and we learn more about the Rot god from
the Blue Dancer Charm.

00:20:11.070 --> 00:20:17.590
"The dancer in blue represents a fairy, who
in legend bestowed a flowing sword upon a

00:20:17.590 --> 00:20:19.510
blind swordsman.

00:20:19.510 --> 00:20:25.120
Blade in hand, the swordsman sealed away an
ancient god — a god that was Rot itself".

00:20:25.120 --> 00:20:32.300
Specifically, this god was sealed away in
the stagnant water downstream of the Ainsel

00:20:32.300 --> 00:20:34.170
River.

00:20:34.170 --> 00:20:43.300
And wherever rot appears, the Kindred of Rot
appear too - pests, and servants of Rot.

00:20:43.300 --> 00:20:49.030
Servants that have now been forsaken by Malenia,
their new goddess

00:20:49.030 --> 00:20:55.200
This blind swordsman with the flowing curved
sword went on to become Malenia's mentor.

00:20:55.200 --> 00:20:59.480
So technically, it's him we have to blame
for this god damned attack.

00:20:59.480 --> 00:21:05.250
The Prosthesis-Wearer Heirloom tells us more:
"A talisman engraved with a scene from a heroic

00:21:05.250 --> 00:21:06.250
tale.

00:21:06.250 --> 00:21:10.480
Though born into the accursed rot, when the
young girl encountered her mentor and his

00:21:10.480 --> 00:21:14.680
flowing blade, she gained wings of unparalleled
strength".

00:21:14.680 --> 00:21:24.410
Aesthetically, it makes a lot of sense that
flowing waters would counter the effects of

00:21:24.410 --> 00:21:25.530
rot.

00:21:25.530 --> 00:21:30.590
For "just as still waters turn foul, stagnation
turns to decay.

00:21:30.590 --> 00:21:33.630
Thus, warriors must remain ever drifting".

00:21:33.630 --> 00:21:37.370
Indeed, Malenia does resist the call of the
rot.

00:21:37.370 --> 00:21:47.570
She does this through sheer will and sense
of self, and only when she is truly pressed

00:21:47.570 --> 00:21:54.130
in battle will she abandon those things, and
bloom into the goddess within.

00:21:54.130 --> 00:22:00.550
Malenia's first bloom was during her fight
against Radahn - a last ditch effort that

00:22:00.550 --> 00:22:05.610
would forever taint the land of Caelid, and
cripple Radahn.

00:22:05.610 --> 00:22:10.240
Whatever she was fighting for in this fight
against Radahn, somehow, it was worth this

00:22:10.240 --> 00:22:12.490
terrible act.

00:22:12.490 --> 00:22:16.380
In general terms at least, it's clear that
Malenia was fighting for her brother.

00:22:16.380 --> 00:22:21.841
Apart from the times where she relapses into
the Goddess of Rot, she is known as the the

00:22:21.841 --> 00:22:23.010
Blade of Miquella.

00:22:23.010 --> 00:22:27.130
She actually goes to great lengths to tell
you this, I don't know if you heard.

00:22:27.130 --> 00:22:33.000
Despite being the toughest boss in From Software
history, she fights for his right to godhood,

00:22:33.000 --> 00:22:34.470
not her own.

00:22:34.470 --> 00:22:39.960
In Malenia's own words, her brother Miquella
"possesses the wisdom, the allure, of a god

00:22:39.960 --> 00:22:43.280
- he is the most fearsome Empyrean of all".

00:22:43.280 --> 00:22:48.170
For his part, Miquella did a lot to earn his
sister's dedication - not the least of which

00:22:48.170 --> 00:22:52.630
was inspiring her armour and a prosthetic
of unalloyed gold.

00:22:52.630 --> 00:22:57.770
And it's not just his sister that loved Miquella
- many people did.

00:22:57.770 --> 00:23:03.970
The Bewitching Branch is an item you can use
to turn enemies into temporary allies, and

00:23:03.970 --> 00:23:08.630
it reads "indeed, he has learned very well
how to compel such affection".

00:23:08.630 --> 00:23:09.762
But hey, maybe he bewitches them for good
reason.

00:23:09.762 --> 00:23:10.762
After all, Miquella is a character that is
defined by the things that he does for others.)

00:23:10.762 --> 00:23:16.400
For his father Radagon, Miquella fashioned
and gifted a fundamentalist incantation called

00:23:16.400 --> 00:23:18.680
"Triple Rings of Light".

00:23:18.680 --> 00:23:24.000
Radagon then returned the favour, gifting
back an incantation called "Radagon's Rings

00:23:24.000 --> 00:23:25.220
of Light".

00:23:25.220 --> 00:23:32.220
These show some of Miquella's positive interactions
with his father and Golden Order fundamentalism.

00:23:32.220 --> 00:23:39.170
"And yet, the young Miquella abandoned fundamentalism,
for it could do nothing to treat Malenia's

00:23:39.170 --> 00:23:40.840
accursed rot.

00:23:40.840 --> 00:23:43.960
This was the beginning of unalloyed gold".

00:23:43.960 --> 00:23:46.720
So..what is unalloyed gold?

00:23:46.720 --> 00:23:54.170
Well, an alloy is a composition of metals
- so unalloyed gold is pure gold, essentially,

00:23:54.170 --> 00:23:58.730
with no external mixtures.

00:23:58.730 --> 00:24:06.480
Fittingly, Miquella bent a lot of his efforts
towards creating an unalloyed gold needle

00:24:06.480 --> 00:24:07.500
- something that could ward away the meddling
of outer gods.

00:24:07.500 --> 00:24:12.380
Specifically, this needle was crafted for
his sister - to ward off the Rot god, and

00:24:12.380 --> 00:24:16.630
forestall the effects of the incurable rotting
sickness .

00:24:16.630 --> 00:24:21.690
We see the bond between the siblings when
we visit Miquella's Haligtree - with a statue

00:24:21.690 --> 00:24:25.620
of a one-armed woman embracing a child.

00:24:25.620 --> 00:24:30.750
In this place, we see the biggest example
of Miquella's benevolence - the Haligtree,

00:24:30.750 --> 00:24:33.920
and the society built into the brace that
supports it.

00:24:33.920 --> 00:24:40.070
This is a promised land seen as a salvation
to many who are shunned or persecuted - provided

00:24:40.070 --> 00:24:43.780
they can find the path here

00:24:43.780 --> 00:24:49.010
Like the other Empyreans, Miquella seems to
have had the will within him to create a new

00:24:49.010 --> 00:24:54.270
order - and it's an order that is somewhat
modeled on those that came before.

00:24:54.270 --> 00:24:59.650
But the biggest thing, is that his Haligtree
is inspired by the Erdtree - but the difference

00:24:59.650 --> 00:25:04.770
is that Miquella's Haligtree is said to be
accepting of all, even those that the Erdtree

00:25:04.770 --> 00:25:06.160
shuns.

00:25:06.160 --> 00:25:10.980
Miquella himself was once embedded inside
of the Haligtree, watering it with his very

00:25:10.980 --> 00:25:13.650
own blood since it was a mere sapling.

00:25:13.650 --> 00:25:18.190
Tragically, however, he was ripped out of
this womb during the shattering - and his

00:25:18.190 --> 00:25:25.390
Haligtree ultimately failed to grow into an
Erdtree, becoming a misshapen husk instead.

00:25:25.390 --> 00:25:27.410
But that's the story for another day.

00:25:27.410 --> 00:25:31.020
There's also a ton of cut content to do with
Miquella.

00:25:31.020 --> 00:25:33.830
Honestly, I've only really laid the foundations
for all the Demi-gods stories' with this video,

00:25:33.830 --> 00:25:36.420
and there's so much yet to come..so subscribe,
and ring the bell -

00:25:36.420 --> 00:25:42.840
Though there is one more thing that I'd like
to mention before I go.

00:25:42.840 --> 00:25:48.190
So...Miquella and Malenia each have their
own butterflies.

00:25:48.190 --> 00:25:53.920
Malenia's is the Aeonian Butterfly, which
inhabit the Swamp of Aeonia, and are rumoured

00:25:53.920 --> 00:25:55.710
to come from the wings of the Goddess of Rot
herself.

00:25:55.710 --> 00:25:56.710
We confirm this when Malenia blooms during
her fight against us, and of course, she bloomed

00:25:56.710 --> 00:25:57.710
previously in Aeonia, in her fight with General
Radahn.

00:25:57.710 --> 00:26:02.640
And I think it's fair to say that Miquella's
butterfly is the Nascent Butterfly, which

00:26:02.640 --> 00:26:08.240
"appears as if it's just emerged from its
cucoon for its entire life".

00:26:08.240 --> 00:26:13.480
This is a reference to Miquella's eternal
youth, and his cuccoon in the Haligtree.

00:26:13.480 --> 00:26:16.150
But there is of course, a third butterfly.

00:26:16.150 --> 00:26:18.890
The Smoldering Butterfly.

00:26:18.890 --> 00:26:22.640
An eternally burning butterfly that serves
as kindling.

00:26:22.640 --> 00:26:27.630
Now bear with me..but it's my theory that
this butterfly is a reference to Melina, who

00:26:27.630 --> 00:26:42.620
the Blade of Calling calls "the kindling maiden",
and "the one who walks alongside flame"..

00:26:42.620 --> 00:26:48.590
At any rate, Melina is almost certainly the
Daughter of Marika - we learned this long

00:26:48.590 --> 00:26:54.690
ago from looking at her name in the game's
files, and can further infer it from her dialogue

00:26:54.690 --> 00:26:58.920
as it refers to mothers.

00:26:58.920 --> 00:27:06.170
Now, this is still just a theory - it's something
that you can choose to believe..but if you

00:27:06.170 --> 00:27:11.180
do choose to believe it, then the fact that
she might have her own butterfly alongside

00:27:11.180 --> 00:27:14.520
Miquella and Malenia might help to confirm
her specific parentage - that being Radagon

00:27:14.520 --> 00:27:20.400
and Marika, which is to say, Marika herself
alone, I guess.

00:27:20.400 --> 00:27:26.190
Honestly, Melina as a character has only become
more mysterious since the game was released,

00:27:26.190 --> 00:27:30.190
and I'm really only scratching the surface
with this theory.

00:27:30.190 --> 00:27:36.020
Speaking of times before Elden Ring was released,
back then, I commissioned this piece from

00:27:36.020 --> 00:27:41.530
a renowned artist named ma-ko..and now I'm
excited to reveal it for the first time!

00:27:41.530 --> 00:27:48.430
This storybook scene is heavily inspired by
the early scenes of Elden Ring, with a red-haired

00:27:48.430 --> 00:27:57.520
protagonist, spirit companions, a mount that
looks like Yakul..and a few more hidden details.

00:27:57.520 --> 00:28:02.290
This piece, and all my other prints are now
available over at Spring, where you can now

00:28:02.290 --> 00:28:07.280
buy them fully framed, and ready to hang.

00:28:07.280 --> 00:28:13.550
The frame itself is in a nice black satin
finish, and you can even opt for a white border

00:28:13.550 --> 00:28:16.610
which looks pretty classy on certain prints.

00:28:16.610 --> 00:28:23.660
I think it's a cool way to support the channel
and artists, and to get something in return

00:28:23.660 --> 00:28:27.820
as well - so check these out, if you're interested.

00:28:27.820 --> 00:28:30.490
But thank you for watching, and I'll see you
next time.

